//@ compile-fail
//@ expect-error: E175
//
// Regression witness for a defect pair that had to be fixed TOGETHER.
//
// Module identity used to be the file BASENAME alone, so this file's aa/helper.sio and
// visibility_basename_collision/helper.sio were ONE module to visibility_allows_access
// (check/check.sio:90, the only caller of ast_path_eq). Two failures rode on that:
//
//   1. OVER-ACCEPTANCE: a private cross-module access between colliding basenames is legal.
//   2. CRASH: when the head bytes compared EQUAL, ast_path_eq fell through to a read of an
//      Option<Box<StringList>> tail — a Box-typed struct field, which Madaros miscompiles —
//      and the compiler SIGSEGVd (rc=139) with no diagnostic at all.
//
// The crash MASKED the over-acceptance. Fixing only the crash turns rc=139 into rc=0, i.e.
// silently accepting the private access — strictly worse. Fixing only identity changes
// nothing, because the comparison crashes before identity matters. Expected: E175.
use visibility_basename_collision::helper::{entry}

fn main() with IO, Mut, Panic {
    print_int(entry())
    println(" must not compile")
}
